bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    jit_block_use_same_name_class_segv_2026-11-27, 0, "Registered 2026-11-27 by p3sweep4 wave-9 lane as the JIT-lane residual of interpreter_lazy_same_name_class_entry_ambiguous_type_2026_11_27: block-scoped use of two lazily loaded same-named classes segfaults (exit 139) on the JIT lane; the interpreter lane resolves correctly after the parent fix. Root-cause direction: block-use arms bind the constructor into the local env + flat MODULE_GLOBALS but record no owner binding, so HIR lowering sees two colliding bare-name classes; fix direction is record_owner_binding in the block-use arms (as evaluation_helpers.rs:72 does for module-scope uses) plus a hir/lower investigation of the crash site. The document remains the authority for diagnosis and acceptance."

